  "title": "A new algorithm can change the pace of evolution",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "bfb44682-12a8-48df-8e59-089fe71c23ca",
      "text": "A new capacity such as a primitive eye does not make mutations more frequent but lets more of them survive: a sighted animal with a bad leg may live where a blind one dies. The surviving changes become material for further evolution, giving the species room to experiment.",
